 ScenarioD;tids;ok;result
⍝ ── D — Deadlock (two locks) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝ ReserveSP and ReservePS take 'SEATS' and 'PAYMENT' in opposite orders. Under load
⍝ each takes its first lock and waits on the other forever. The harness runs both under
⍝ a 1008 guard, gives them a moment, then treats any thread still alive as deadlocked
⍝ and kills it. It checks ⎕TNUMS rather than ⎕TSYNC, which would hang on a blocked
⍝ thread. Your own flows carry no guard: the aim is to see the DEADLOCK (1008) and
⍝ design it out. Do not :Trap it, since a trapped thread stays suspended with its token
⍝ still held.
 NewSeats 1000
 DEADLOCK←0
 tids←({1008::DEADLOCK←1 ⋄ ⊢ReserveSP ⍵}&0),({1008::DEADLOCK←1 ⋄ ⊢ReservePS ⍵}&0)
 {}⎕DL 0.5                          ⍝ let the flows reach the deadlock (main thread idle)
 :If ∨/tids∊⎕TNUMS ⋄ {}⎕TKILL tids ⋄ DEADLOCK←1 ⋄ :EndIf   ⍝ still blocked ⇒ deadlock
 ok←0=DEADLOCK
 result←'FAIL' 'PASS'⊃⍨⎕IO+ok
 ⎕←'D deadlock    : deadlocked = ',⍕DEADLOCK
 ⎕←'Scenario D: ',result
